bugs.summary:
You strip '<script><!--
// Don't remove
var x = 1;
//--></script><p>Welcome to our store</p>' with HTMLStripCharFilter and expect 'Welcome to our store', which is what you get without the apostrophe and what the filter's own tests expect after wrapped script and style blocks. Instead the output is empty: inside the <!-- --> section the apostrophe opens a quoted-string state that ignores '-->' and '</script>', and because the input ends in that state everything after the quote is dropped, so the text is never indexed and a TermQuery for a word after the block misses the document. The same happens with an apostrophe in a CSS comment of a wrapped <style> block or with a lone '"', with no error.
